---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Pagination from "../../components/Pagination.astro";
import Picture from "../../components/Picture.astro";
import BrowserFrame from "../../components/BrowserFrame.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="GTreasury" pathname="/work/gtreasury/" caseStudy={true}>
  <div class="case-study">
    <div class="case-study-header">
      <div class="case-study-header-content constrain">
        <h1>GTreasury</h1>
        <div class="case-study-header-nav">
          <a title="Previous" href="/work/material-palettes/"
            ><Pagination name="previous" /></a
          >
          <a title="Next" href="/work/balto/"><Pagination name="next" /></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="case-study-overview">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Role:</strong> UX engineer (design systems + prototyping)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Challenge:</strong> Six disconnected codebases and conflicting UX
          patterns causing fragmented workflows and high error rates.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Top outcome:</strong> Created and deployed the Obelisk design system
          (40+ components), unifying all product lines ahead of a major platform modernization
          and $1B acquisition.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="case-study-content pswp-gallery">
      <h2>From fragments to a shared system</h2>
      <p>
        GTreasury’s product ecosystem had grown through years of acquisitions.
        Five product lines lived across six codebases, each with different
        frameworks, visual languages, and interaction patterns. This
        fragmentation increased user error rates and made basic financial tasks
        tedious to complete.
      </p>
      <p>
        Working alongside a UX researcher, I audited the platform to identify
        reusable interface patterns. The goal was to establish a design system
        that could drive modernization without forcing product teams to rebuild
        from scratch.
      </p>
      <div class="case-study-image-block">
        <figure class="case-study-image-solo">
          <Picture
            name="gt-brainstorm"
            alt="Sticky notes mapping shared UI patterns across legacy products"
            caption="Auditing shared interface patterns and synthesizing research
            findings."
            showCaption={false}
            lightbox
          />
          <figcaption class="case-study-image-caption">
            Auditing shared interface patterns and synthesizing research
            findings.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <h2>Building Obelisk</h2>
      <p>
        I led the creation of Obelisk, a Figma design system structured around
        design tokens, reusable components, and complex multi-state patterns. It
        expanded to 40+ core components, including dense data tables, complex
        forms, and financial dashboards.
      </p>
      <p>
        Rather than treating Obelisk as a visual reference, I structured it for
        direct engineering handoff. Token naming, variables, and component
        properties were aligned to match frontend architecture, establishing a
        shared translation layer between design and code.
      </p>
      <div class="case-study-image-block">
        <figure>
          <div class="case-study-image-grid">
            <Picture
              name="gt-palette"
              alt="Color palette token hierarchy and variable definitions in the Obelisk design system"
              caption="Obelisk color system: Defining scales and semantic tokens for neutral, primary, success, warning, and failure modes."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="gt-buttons"
              alt="Button component variants, sizes, and interactive states in Figma"
              caption="Button component spec: Mapping interactive hover, active, and disabled states."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="gt-wizard"
              alt="Multi-step wizard modal component layout with progress indicators"
              caption="Multi-step wizard: Building higher-order setup flows using upstream tokens."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="gt-table"
              alt="Dense financial data table component with labels"
              caption="Data table component: Demonstrating density, total functionality, and edge cases."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="case-study-image-caption">
            Core design tokens and multi-state UI components built for dense
            enterprise workflows in Obelisk.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <h2>Validating through prototyping</h2>
      <p>
        To prove the system in practice, we applied Obelisk to high-friction
        workflows like payment creation and cash worksheet management. I
        translated research insights into high-fidelity Figma prototypes,
        testing complex states and dense data layouts.
      </p>
      <p>
        Next, I partnered with frontend engineering to build a <a
          href="https://gtreasury.netlify.app/dashboard"
          >production-ready Angular prototype</a
        >. Writing the underlying Sass and component logic allowed us to solve
        layout constraints, accessibility edge cases, and interactive states
        before touching production code.
      </p>
      <div class="case-study-image-block">
        <figure>
          <div class="case-study-image-grid">
            <Picture
              name="gt-form"
              alt="High-fidelity deal creation form layout in Figma"
              caption="Financial deal creation layout: Optimizing tab order, field grouping, and inline validation for rapid data entry."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
            <Picture
              name="gt-worksheet-i18n"
              alt="Internationalized cash positioning worksheet prototype with multi-currency data"
              caption="Cash positioning worksheet: Stress-testing dense financial grids against internationalized formatting."
              showCaption={false}
              lightbox
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="case-study-image-caption">
            High-fidelity Figma prototypes evaluating complex form structures
            and internationalized worksheet flows.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="case-study-image-block">
        <figure>
          <BrowserFrame
            title="gtreasury.netlify.app"
            url="https://gtreasury.netlify.app/financial-instruments/portfolios"
          />
          <figcaption class="case-study-image-caption">
            Interactive prototype executing live Obelisk tokens, Sass
            architecture, and component state logic in the browser.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <h2>Modernizing a monolith</h2>
      <p>
        Obelisk was deployed across all five product lines, with over half of
        its 40+ components shared globally across teams. It gave design and
        engineering a unified vocabulary, drastically reducing redundant
        component development across legacy codebases.
      </p>
      <p>
        The system established the design and implementation foundation for
        GTreasury’s platform modernization, positioning the product line ahead
        of its $1B acquisition.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
